cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  companion paper (see preferred-citation).
type: software
title: "acropora: computing statistical solutions of nonlinear partial differential equations"
abstract: >-
  Computing statistical solutions of nonlinear partial differential
  equations via Monte Carlo ensembles on CPU
  (NumPy) and GPU (CuPy), with reproducible stochastic initial data.
  First scheme: a vectorial lattice Boltzmann method for the compressible
  Euler equations; reference application: statistical solutions of a
  Mach 2000 astrophysical jet.
authors:
  - family-names: Simonis
    given-names: Stephan
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-17"
license: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
repository-code: "https://github.com/stephan-911/acropora"
keywords:
  - statistical solutions
  - measure-valued solutions
  - lattice Boltzmann method
  - compressible Euler equations
  - Monte Carlo
  - astrophysical jets
  - GPU computing
